        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.11,
            0.883,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The famous pyramids in Egypt have square bases. The puzzle in Fig. 14.11B (made by the Hungarian architect Erno Rubik) has a triangular base."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.167,
            0.884,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some mountains have pyramidal peaks (formed by glacier erosion over many millennia). In India, there is the Shivling Peak in the state of Uttarakhand. An example from the Alps is the Matterhorn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.233,
            0.479,
            0.414
          ],
          "content": [
            {
